	(text "RESET, RUN, PAUSE, LOAD: THE BOOT RESET, CLEAR / WAIT, THE DMA INTERLOCK, LOADED" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 12.7 0) (effects (font (size 2.5 2.5) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "724d5e07-7c4f-5dc9-9fe4-0f94990d2a7f"))
	(text "CLEAR = -RESET and WAIT = -PAUSE, each through two Schmitt inverters: reset, run, pause (-PAUSE low) and load (both\nlow) follow directly. U10 DS1813 on -RESET holds it low 150 ms after whatever pulled it lets go (no watchdog).\nA boot reset is a state of the bus (2026-11-22): -RESET and -DMAIN low with -PAUSE high. SW1 RESET and power-on\n(U12, a DS1813 on SW_RST) make it through U11A / U11B (74HC03, open drain; U11B not while -PAUSE is low); the\nfront panel's RESET button and the bus driver make it from outside. BOOT_L (U6B) clears LOADED (U8A); LOAD mode\nsets it. LED6 (on U8A's Q through R8) is lit while it is set: the next RUN starts in RAM at 0000, not in the EPROM.\nDMA IN = -DMAIN only once DMA_ARMED (U8B): -PAUSE low, and -DMAIN seen high since (U11D, U9A; U11C with R9)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 17.78 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid "abba7627-7abb-5343-bc1e-c7eacfd5d2e2"))
	(embedded_fonts no)
)
